b.com/openfootmanager/openfootmanager/commit/b7b959518d702501d59106e0cbe2af49ab3f2844","commit_subject":"docs(types): a response type outside Game and SquadPlayer is added to the roots","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"rvdbreemen/OTGW-firmware","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:48:57Z","branch":"dev","commit_sha":"443a3c3213b1a6c525af5d85a1c0cbb6793eb237","github_link":"https://github.com/rvdbreemen/OTGW-firmware/commit/443a3c3213b1a6c525af5d85a1c0cbb6793eb237","commit_subject":"fix(update): TASK-1534 /update flash utility page links back to the web UI","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:48:56Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"7db28e62a2b689ab537d2e0c1e25055d502e7b6e","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/7db28e62a2b689ab537d2e0c1e25055d502e7b6e","commit_subject":"The server reads and writes its session records, its last virtual IPs and its configuration-error strike without blocking a thread. SessionLocalService takes an async lock rather than a sync one and writes a record whole under the caller's token, and a record that is asked for has its time touched rather than being rewritten. VirtualIpManager reads its last IPs at the first allocation, their only use, rather than in its constructor, and saves new IPs before it takes them as allocated; ConfigErrorTracker reads its strike file at the first error, likewise, so VpnHoodServer's constructor reads no file and needs no async Create. The session lifecycle is async with them: creating, recovering and removing a session, the cleanup, and ISessionResponseHandler.ApplySessionResponses, which the usage reporter awaits. The recovery at the start lets a cancel through rather than logging it as a session it could not add","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"FabMo/FabMo-Engine","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T20:48:54Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"9eea73648de5c9f7503771ad94eeae9116a67355","github_link":"https://github.com/FabMo/FabMo-Engine/commit/9eea7